================================================================================
THE VENDORED JOURNAL, AND THE MIT CODE IT CARRIES
================================================================================

`vendor/thebes-ledger-core/` is the double-entry journal this layer consumes
(`src/journal/`, Apache-2.0, Thebes Core Team) together with the ledger family it
builds on (`src/ledger/`, MIT) and two derivative works of that family
(`src/facade/`). It is vendored as source so that this repository builds on its
own.

MIT-licensed files in `vendor/thebes-ledger-core/src/ledger/`, taken from the
ICRC-ME ledger (Copyright (c) 2026 Mercatura Forum, MIT):

  Allowances.mo  Archive.mo  BTreeIndex.mo  BlockLog.mo  BloomFilter.mo
  CBOR.mo  CertifiedTree.mo  IndexedLedger.did  IndexedLedger.mo
  MerkleMMR.mo  RegionBTree.mo  RegionBalances.mo  StableLog.mo  Types.mo

`MerkleMMR.mo` carries one recorded change in `verifyProof` (the multi-peak fold
order); every other file above is the upstream file unchanged.

Derivative works of that MIT code, which carry the same MIT copyright and
permission notice for the derived portions alongside this repository's
Apache-2.0 licence for what was added:

  vendor/thebes-ledger-core/src/facade/TokenLedger.mo   derived from IndexedLedger.mo
  vendor/thebes-ledger-core/src/facade/FacadeCert.mo    reproduces CertifiedTree.mo's tip tree
  vendor/thebes-ledger-core/src/ledger/RegionIndex.mo   derived from RegionBTree.mo: per-index
                                                        key and value widths, a sibling pointer
                                                        in the node header, a cursor-resumable
                                                        range, a page free list, and a
                                                        right-edge split

Everything else in this repository (`src/`, `test/`, `integration/`, `tools/`,
`vendor/thebes-ledger-core/src/journal/`, and the two further files in
`vendor/thebes-ledger-core/src/ledger/`, `ByteBuf.mo` and `RegionRebuild.mo`) is
original work under Apache-2.0. Where a module reproduces a construction from one of the MIT files
rather than calling it, the file and the construction are named in that
module's header comment.

